# Keep the build context minimal and deterministic. The Dockerfile regenerates
# all browser assets from the published packages, so local/generated copies and
# the local-dev workspace file must not leak into the image build.
.git
.github
.gitignore
.dockerignore
*.md
build/
node_modules/
web-terminal-server-bin
go.work
go.work.sum
static/vendor/
static/style.css
# The css-bundle temp sibling. Load-bearing rather than tidy: a leftover in the
# build context reaches COPY . ./ and then `go:embed static`, so it would ship
# inside the binary.
static/style.css.*
# Skill artifact trees. They cache-bust COPY . ./ on every review checkpoint and
# are excluded from git for the same reason.
**/.code-review/
**/.judgement/
**/.app-review/
# scripts/ is deliberately NOT excluded: the wire-floor gate compiles
# scripts/wirecheck inside the builder stage, so it must be in the build
# context. Only the built binary is copied into the final image.
#
# A LOCAL build of it at the repo root is a different matter: 6 MB of host-arch
# binary that the builder would ship into its context and then ignore.
/wirecheck
